      {
        "claim": "Lifecycle wiring always resolves across the artifact union ([issue #114](https://github.com/yestechgroup/rexlang/issues/114)): a capability clause names a declared capability; a granted or delegated capability is carried by an operation or search; an `.ifml` action declaration binds to a service operation (case-insensitive verb equality); a subscription consumer names a declared deploy component; flow `requires:`/`roles:` resolve into the actor layer; an operation's `emits` event name is declared in some `.evt` contract; a declared event is emitted by at least one service operation (channel `publishes`/subscription lists are consumption-side and never satisfy production). Since rexlang#128 the two capability joins resolve at **compile time** (rule 10 pooling every provided actor model, with the `unknownCapability` did-you-mean code; grant coverage in the actor engine, code `grantedCapabilityUncarried`) — the union pass keeps them as its lint channel (warning severity). Every union-pass diagnostic carries its stable registry code prefixed on the message (`X0001`–`X0008`, the `driver.integrity` band of [the diagnostic-code registry](DIAGNOSTICS.md)), and an action whose case-insensitive mirror matches **several** service operations binds to no unique backend — an error (`X0006`), the mirror naming exactly one `(service, operation)` carrier",
