      {
        "claim": "Stripped-name uniqueness within a package (issue #177): two declarations — classes or enums, in any combination — whose names strip to the same module identifier (one trailing `Type` suffix, then snake_case; `PayRun` and `PayRunType` both strip to `pay_run`), or two classes mapping to the same effective table name (declared `table \"…\"` override, else the derived default), are rejected; a pair where either class is a containment target is exempt (a contained value object shares its owner's module downstream by design), and a pair already diagnosed as E0300 is not re-diagnosed as E0301 (one rename resolves both)",
